UNIT ringToken
KIND FUNCTIONAL
FIDELITY spec
SIG ringToken(items, gate) -> Promise<Array>
DESCRIPTION Appends each item to a result array, coordinating access through a single
DESCRIPTION circulating permission (a "token") so that only one actor acts at a time.
DESCRIPTION Each append is performed by awaiting `gate.open(item)`; the gate resolves it.
DESCRIPTION The token is manipulated through `gate.token`, which offers exactly three calls:
DESCRIPTION   gate.token.take(who)         — actor `who` acquires the permission
DESCRIPTION   gate.token.pass(from, to)    — `from` hands the permission to `to`
DESCRIPTION   gate.token.release(who)      — `who` gives the permission back
DESCRIPTION Actors are identified by their index in `items` (0, 1, 2, …).
DESCRIPTION Export the function as the DEFAULT export. No imports of any kind.
RING the token circulates in index order: 0 takes it, passes to 1, 1 passes to 2, …
INVARIANT the result is the items in INDEX ORDER (the token order determines it).
INVARIANT MUTUAL EXCLUSION: at most ONE actor holds the token at any instant. Actor 0
INVARIANT   TAKES it; every later actor RECEIVES it via pass(from, to) — never take().
INVARIANT NO LOSS: the permission is released exactly once at the end, by the LAST actor,
INVARIANT   so that no actor still holds it when the unit returns.
INVARIANT an empty items array returns [] and touches neither gate.open nor gate.token.
